  "name": "VRview Plugin - Cross-Site Scripting",
  "author": "ritikchaddha",
  "severity": "HIGH",
  "description": "The VRview plugin is a tool commonly used to embed and display 360-degree virtual reality content in web applications. However, improper input sanitization in the plugin allows attackers to inject malicious scripts into trusted websites. This vulnerability, classified as Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), could enable attackers to perform unauthorized actions or steal sensitive user data.\n",
